                                "exploitable": true,
                                "platform": "android",
                                "remediation": "If no app data should be backed up, set the `android:allowBackup` attribute to `\"false\"` under the `<application ... >` tag in the AndroidManifest.xml file.\nIf certain files are allowed to be backed up, explicitly define backup rules to limit data exposure. Use the `android:dataExtractionRules` attribute for Android 12 and above, or `android:fullBackupContent` for Android 11 and below. Ensure that only essential files are included in these rules to prevent unintended data from being backed up.",
